+D.9.8 Scope, verification and references
+The pseudoinverse, whitening and Gaussian arguments are standard statistical linear algebra.
+The specialized results here are their application to the declared gluing observation, its exact
+spectra, the fixed-norm degenerating family and the exact canonical sampling contract. Con-
+structor replay supplies exact characteristic-polynomial/LDL/Sturm certificates plus separately
+labelled floating fixtures. It does not estimate a physical noise covariance, establish independent
+review, certify measured bandwidth or prove a physical entropy-area relation.
+Primary background: LAPACK Users’ Guide, Linear Least Squares Problems, and How to
+Measure Errors. General perturbation literature includes G. W. Stewart, On the Perturbation
+of Pseudo-Inverses, Projections and Linear Least Squares Problems; only its abstract/metadata
+were inspected, so no specific theorem from its paywalled text is invoked here. The displayed
+bounds have self-contained proofs.
+Next requirements for operational use are calibrated joint covariance, acquisition and clock-error
+models, admissible sampling windows, generator uncertainty and a complete resource ledger.
+The derivation closes a mathematical conditioning gap while leaving those physical inputs ex-
+plicit.
